<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">Italo-Turkish War</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1911–1912</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Italo-Turkish War of 1911–1912 was fought between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ottoman-empire">Ottoman Empire</a>. Italy seized Tripolitania and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cyrenaica">Cyrenaica</a>, which became the colony of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/libya">Libya</a>, along with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dodecanese">Dodecanese</a> islands. The war expanded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-empire">Italian Empire</a> and saw early military use of aircraft.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/italo-turkish-war.jpg" alt="Italo-Turkish War" width="320" height="314" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: File:Turkish prisoners Rhodes 1912.jpg: L'Illustrazione italiana, 16 June 1912. File:Atatürk 1912.jpg: Bilinmiyor Fil... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Italo-Turkish_war_collage.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
